.TH geectl-request-file-maintenance-incident 1  "geectl-request-file-maintenance-incident 0.2.2" 
.SH NAME
geectl\-request\-file\-maintenance\-incident \- File a maintenance incident request: ask the maintenance team to start a maintenance incident from a maintenance update
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgeectl request file\-maintenance\-incident\fR [\fB\-\-source\-package\fR] [\fB\-\-release\-project\fR] [\fB\-\-with\-cleanup\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fB\-\-source\-project\fR> <\fB\-\-target\-project\fR> <\fB\-\-description\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
File a maintenance incident request: ask the maintenance team to start a maintenance incident from a maintenance update
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-source\-project\fR \fI<SOURCE_PROJECT>\fR
The project the maintenance update comes from
.TP
\fB\-\-source\-package\fR \fI<SOURCE_PACKAGE>\fR
A package in the source project. Repeatable: one action per package; at least one is required
.TP
\fB\-\-target\-project\fR \fI<TARGET_PROJECT>\fR
The maintenance project the incident goes to
.TP
\fB\-\-release\-project\fR \fI<RELEASE_PROJECT>\fR
The release project the update releases into. When omitted, the server resolves it from the maintenance project
.TP
\fB\-\-description\fR \fI<DESCRIPTION>\fR
The request description. Values starting with `\-` are taken literally: a description may open with a `\- ` bullet
.TP
\fB\-\-with\-cleanup\fR
Delete the source branch when the incident is accepted. By default the branch survives the incident
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SH VERSION
v0.2.2
